Package: aurora-system-fixes
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends: systemd, udev, bluez (>= 5.87), ethtool, iw, procps,
 aurora-panel-nits, aurora-nvram, aurora-btsync, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Aurora system drop-ins awaiting named upstream fixes
 systemd, udev, libinput and GSettings defaults for Apple Silicon Macs, each
 waiting for a named upstream fix or recording a platform decision:
  - the hardware model and vendor names from the firmware, unmangled;
  - the render-only GPU card left alone by mutter;
  - wake for network access while on the power adapter, as on macOS;
  - trackpad clicks played by the host where the trackpad has an actuator;
  - no libinput palm size threshold where the kernel decides palms by size;
  - the Mission Control key opening the GNOME overview;
  - a reboot or kexec watchdog within the Apple watchdog's range;
  - PCIe ASPM substates and no realtime utilization floor;
  - ordering fixes for DrKonqi's user units, the NetworkManager dispatcher
    and a second Btrfs swapfile.
